A||||8||Dan Robinson||Opposites don't Attract ! !  (in my case)||||9||
Z||000000||Dan Robinson||09-26-2001||06:54 PM||||I am replacing my 2.5 Duke for a 2.8 six, but the 2.8 six is from an automatic and I have a manual tranny.  What all do I have to do to change the engine to stick? ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-26-2001||07:55 PM||||I think all you need is the ECM from a manual.  However, the only thing the autos have that is different from a manual is the TCC....I think.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-26-2001||08:28 PM||||Actually, Leadfoot, the entire tranny is different, not just the TCC.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||09:48 PM||||Yes, I'm pretty sure the clutch is also different, maybe even the shift cables....<P>Do a search on conversion, there's more reading material on the subject than you have time. GL||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||09-26-2001||10:59 PM||||You need a flywheel for the V-6, clutch, engine harness for a manual transmission, air cleaner assy., ECM, some modifications to the exhaust or a new one (including tips) and dog bone. Don't forget to change the fuel pump out! I think that's about it.<BR>OH, good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan Robinson||09-27-2001||03:03 AM||||So, am I gonna need a new bell housing?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000006||artherd||09-27-2001||03:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dan Robinson:<BR><B>So, am I gonna need a new bell housing?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In a manner of speaking...<P>(Fieros don't have bellhousings, at least, not as distinct from the transmissions themselves, they're one piece ;)<P>There should be several auto-&gt;manual conversion full writeups in the archives.  It's involved,  but not TOO hard ;)<P>Good luck!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Fie Ro||09-27-2001||04:23 PM||||I think a V6 clutch is different so you will need one (or replace it while this is good moment)...shift cables can be different and check whether your current trans can handle the "power" of the V6....you also need ECM and all wiring of the V6. Don't forget enginemounts & dogbone may be different! Sometimes (mostly) it's easier/cheaper to buy a V6 car instead of of changing a 4 to a 6....<BR><P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan Robinson||09-27-2001||06:43 PM||||Thanks everybody.<P>Hey Fie Ro I snagged a '88 2.8 w/ 88,000 for $99.00 and my mechanic says it will run me around the $1,000 ballpark for the install.  The reason I'm doing this is my Duke cried for mercy and died, so I'm going to just put the six in. ||||reg||10
